<title>USA: Chartwell Leisure Q1 shr loss $0.25.</title>
<headline>Chartwell Leisure Q1 shr loss $0.25.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the Three Month	For the Three Month  Pro Forma</p>
<p>								 Three</p>
<p>								 Month</p>
<p>     Period Ended		 Period Ended    Period Ended</p>
<p>    March 31, 1997	   March 31, 1996    March 31, 1996(A)</p>
<p>Revenues (000) $25,514	  $13,865	    $24,607</p>
<p>ADR (B)	   $52.88	   $56.98	     $51.01</p>
<p>Occupancy (B)    57.0%	    62.0%		57.2%</p>
<p>Rev Par (B)     $30.17	   $35.33		$29.17</p>
<p>Net Loss (000) $(2,797)	 $(1,930)	    $(2,921)</p>
<p>Loss Per Share   $(.25)	   $(.33)		$(.50)</p>
<p>EBITDA before</p>
<p>charge for office</p>
<p> relocation (000)$2,250     $1,307 (C)	    $2,446(C)</p>
<p>A) The pro forma financial data has been presented to reflect the results of the company's business operations as if the company's acquisition of the stock of Forte Hotels Inc, the company's acquisition of interests in 21 hotels from Capital Properties Limited Partnership and the company's sale of  4.0 million common shares o Chartwell Leisure Associates, L.P. II and FSNL LLC and related use of proceeds had occurred on January 1, 1996.</p>
<p>B) Reflects hotels operated for at least twelve months.</p>
<p>C) EBITDA for 1996 is before non-cash provision for loss on</p>
<p>gaming assets.</p>
<p>Full company name is Chartwell Leisure Inc,</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
